    <p>On Village Street, Harvington. Regular users include Harvey Bears Nursery and Pre-School, exercise classes, Girlguiding groups and village clubs. See <a href="{{ '/regulars/' | url }}">Regular activities</a> for days and times.</p>
    <h3>Hire the hall</h3>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ contacts.orgs['village-hall'].email }}">{{ contacts.orgs['village-hall'].email }}</a> or call the Booking Secretary on {{ contacts.orgs['village-hall'].phone }}. Hire rates are on the noticeboard outside the hall.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="norton">
    <h2>Norton and Lenchwick Parish Hall</h2>
    <div class="gallery gallery-one">
      <figure><img src="{{ '/images/photos/norton-and-lenchwick-norton-and-lenchwick-village-hall-1.webp' | url }}" alt="Norton and Lenchwick Parish Hall, a single-storey brick building with a car park" width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy"><figcaption class="small muted">Norton and Lenchwick Parish Hall, Byrd Row</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <p>At 2 Byrd Row, Norton, the hall for Norton and Lenchwick. Regular users include St Egwin's Craft Group, a fortnightly coffee morning and the u3a's short mat bowls, and it has table tennis equipment for anyone wanting to start a group. See <a href="{{ '/regulars/' | url }}">Regular activities</a> for days and times.</p>
    <h3>Hire the hall</h3>
    <p>Call the Bookings Administrator on {{ contacts.orgs['norton-hall'].phone }}.</p>
